## 8. Interview Questions

**Q1. What is alert triage?**  
Alert triage is the initial process of reviewing and prioritizing alerts to decide which require further investigation.

**Q2. Does a failed SSH login prove brute-force activity?**  
No. Repeated failures from the same source over a short period may indicate brute-force activity, but context and supporting evidence are needed.

**Q3. What is event correlation?**  
It is the process of connecting related events using fields such as timestamps, IP addresses, usernames, and hostnames.

**Q4. Why is incident documentation important?**  
It preserves evidence, explains the investigation, supports escalation, and helps other analysts understand the decision.

**Q5. Why might the Wazuh Dashboard be unavailable even when the Manager is active?**  
The Dashboard depends on other services, including the Indexer. A failed Indexer can prevent the Dashboard from retrieving and displaying data.

